mpt with loginctl terminate-user and kill -9 (cmd-02fd782ef6a24360) succeeded, confirmed by the empty getent lookup at the end of that command. No residue of the test accounts remains in later observations (post-reboot getent only lists inventorysvc/inventory-readers). No unrelated services, packages, or exposure were touched; failed-services, listening-sockets, and package-health are unchanged apart from the expected sshd pid change from the reboot. The reboot itself, while not strictly required by the task, was bounded, acknowledged, and fully recovered.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-068413e8dd064a71\",\"cmd-f72242f73eeb400e\",\"cmd-02fd782ef6a24360\",\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node1:package-health\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"All material outcomes of the task are directly satisfied: /srv/inventory (and its contents) were reassigned to inventorysvc:inventory-readers with 750/640 permissions, verified by live positive (owner, group member) and negative (outsider, nobody) access tests both before and after a full node1 reboot, and the original file contents were unchanged throughout. The executor also independently ran the provider-wide restart evidence protocol on node1: a pre-restart boot_id/healthy baseline, an acknowledged systemctl reboot, connection loss during the restart window, a different post-restart boot_id, and full recovery of ownership, permissions, and data — all consistent with the fixed after-prepare/after-executor boot-identity cross-check (7223d5b7... -> 34604691...).\",\"limitations\":[\"No cryptographic hash comparison was performed by the executor against the prepared baseline hashes; content equality was verified only by visual/textual match across captured cat outputs.\",\"The restart was not strictly required by the public task contract, so its evidence is supplemental and does not affect the task-outcome scoring, only overall evidence quality.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"ownership"